{
    "article_summary": "The article describes the first catalytic protocol for the direct intermolecular C-H trifluoromethoxylation of (hetero)arenes. Using a novel N-OCF3 reagent (1) and redox-active catalysts like Ru(bpy)3(PF6)2 under 402 nm LED irradiation, the method proceeds at room temperature with high functional group tolerance. Mechanistic studies indicate that photoexcitation of reagent 1 generates OCF3 radicals, which are trapped by arenes, followed by catalyst-mediated SET and deprotonation to yield the trifluoromethoxylated products.",
